hadiths[1]{hadithnumber,text}:
"1307","Abdul-Jabbar bin Al-Ala told us, Sufyan told us, he said: I did not memorize it from Al-Zuhri except on the authority of Saeed, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, he said: Omar passed, With Hassan, while he was singing in the mosque, he noticed him and said: I was singing and there was someone better than you in it, then he turned to Abu Hurairah and said: I adjure you by God, did you hear the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, saying: “Answer on my behalf, O God, support him with the Holy Spirit?” He said: Yes. And he narrated to us, saying: Al-Hasan bin Al-Sabbah Al-Bazzar, and Sa’id bin Abdul-Rahman, commended him, saying: Sufyan narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, something similar to this, Saeed said: I used to sing during it, and there is someone better than you in it, and Al-Hasan said: I used to sing during it for someone who is better than you."
